    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s optimal lineup for July 12th leans heavily into high-contact, high-floor profiles against favorable arm matchups. The strongest play of the day is **Daulton Varsho** (69.56), who benefits from a prime matchup against M\u00e1rquez. While the opposing pitcher's xERA of 5.58 is the primary driver, **Varsho**\u2019s +10% dynamic platoon boost makes him our highest-projected asset today. He is closely shadowed by **Taylor Ward** (68.88) and **Dylan Beavers** (68.38), both of whom capitalize on a significant +16% park factor boost against Lugo. **Luis Arraez** (65.86) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (62.57) also see their stocks rise significantly due to a +18% SP Skill bump against Lorenzen, solidifying the heart of our lineup as a high-efficiency engine for AVG and R.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved leaving **Bryce Harper** (50.42) on the bench. Despite his elite 0.394 xwOBA, the data necessitates a pivot because of the brutal matchup against Skubal, whose 2.69 xERA acts as a massive anchor on his scoring potential. By comparison, **Drew Gilbert** (51.55) actually outscored **Harper** in our efficiency model due to the more favorable soft-toss matchup against Lorenzen, though he ultimately remained on the pine due to his bottom-of-the-order positioning. We are keeping a close eye on **JJ Bleday**; while he sports a respectable 53.63, the matchup against Boyd requires caution, as the southpaw-on-southpaw dynamic limits his upside despite the park advantage. We are rolling with these starters, prioritizing the sustained efficiency of **Varsho** and **Ward** to keep our Roto standing stable.",
